WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.250
The book's decision matrix runs
on one rule: one decider per row.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.656
The single deliberate
exception is the pilot gate,

3
00:00:07.656 --> 00:00:10.575
G2, which the steward
and the sponsor co-sign.

4
00:00:10.575 --> 00:00:15.753
The sponsor and the CIO own scope, funding
and sequence, break ties, and decide

5
00:00:15.753 --> 00:00:21.425
when Active Directory components retire,
because each retirement ends a fallback.

6
00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:24.606
They clear gate G3 with
the steering committee,

7
00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:27.950
and G5, the retirement of
Active Directory itself.

8
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:32.612
Their job is to keep it a program, not
five projects that finish one at a time.

9
00:00:32.612 --> 00:00:37.087
The CISO decides the control
requirements every surface must meet.

10
00:00:37.087 --> 00:00:42.130
The authorizing official is the only
official who can accept risk on the agency's

11
00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:47.323
behalf, so every place the program carries
risk instead of removing it reaches that

12
00:00:47.323 --> 00:00:50.259
desk: a deferred
legacy-authentication cutoff,

13
00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:54.775
a Kerberos island with no end date, a
deviation from a mandatory baseline.

14
00:00:54.775 --> 00:00:58.625
The program office, led by the
steward, runs the orchestra.

15
00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:03.124
It holds the repository, turns
assessments into authorized plans

16
00:01:03.124 --> 00:01:07.050
and evaluates the gates, but it
doesn't decide risk or scope.

17
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:10.287
The platform teams do the
work inside each domain.

18
00:01:10.287 --> 00:01:13.737
Application owners decide
for their own applications.

19
00:01:13.737 --> 00:01:16.437
HR decides what the
worker attributes mean.

20
00:01:16.437 --> 00:01:21.455
The sponsor's decision, before the program
starts: fill in the matrix with names,

21
00:01:21.455 --> 00:01:24.233
one decider per row,
and get the authorizing

22
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:27.530
official's agreement to
every risk-acceptance row.
